1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Round two, match one of the Royal Knight Selection Exam.

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Team B was at a distinct disadvantage against Kirsch's overwhelming magic might.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Black Hurricane!

7
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,000
But Asta channeled his dark power to nullify Kirsch's spells in one fell swoop,

8
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:51,000
along with some traps the mysterious mage Zerks had set up before the exam.

9
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Now they're back to square one.

10
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,000
There's only one way to beat a team as strong as that, and guess what?

11
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:58,000
It's by making a team that's stronger!

12
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,000
I guess that leaves me with no choice but to put you to use.

13
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Working together for the first time, Zora and Asta set up an ingenious snare

14
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
that successfully lured in the self-absorbed Kirsch, and removed him from the battlefield.

15
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,000
I told you that you and me could make a good team!

16
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Make a good team!

17
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Hit!

18
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:16,000
�-

19
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,000
skigきき...

20
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:30,000
君のこと

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,020
哇-Wow-Wow-Wow-Wow-かなかったから

22
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,000
trustworthy to make a interface

23
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Okay.

24
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:17,780
Thank you.

25
00:02:17,780 --> 00:02:18,920
No, no, no!

26
00:02:48,780 --> 00:02:54,580
Okay, according to my magic flower guidepost, the enemy hid their crystal inside of Sol's golem.

27
00:02:58,300 --> 00:03:03,460
If I use this seed to plant my magic-controlling weeds inside of Sol's spell, we can win this!

28
00:03:03,840 --> 00:03:08,280
It'll let me take control of her little mud pet long enough to expose the gem and shatter it.

29
00:03:08,540 --> 00:03:15,260
The problem is, that spell needs time to sprout and put down roots, and I'd have to fight it though I didn't know the seed was sown.

30
00:03:15,260 --> 00:03:18,020
Will I be able to pull off a feint like that?

31
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:22,400
Plant magic! Magic cannon flower!

32
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:26,800
You're not as weak as I thought, but not good enough!

33
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:29,020
Earth magic! Cloth seal!

34
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:35,660
I want to win, but I'm not into hurting women.

35
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:37,400
How about you stay out of this?

36
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:39,340
They have to warn the others!

37
00:03:39,860 --> 00:03:43,160
Now then, I wonder how far that hothead can get on his own.

38
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:48,180
It was only a matter of time before your overconfidence led to your downfall.

39
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:50,080
And now, look at you.

40
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:53,700
I can't believe you fell for such a primitive trap.

41
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:55,600
Are you really a vice-captain?

42
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,760
Save some face and quit already.

43
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:01,420
Egotistical morons like you make me sick.

44
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:04,220
By the way, your precious face is all scratched up.

45
00:04:04,220 --> 00:04:07,760
Why are you piling the insults on a guy who's totally out cold?

46
00:04:08,140 --> 00:04:09,620
Still, this was a great idea.

47
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:12,260
May have been a bit risky, but that pitfall worked out in the end.

48
00:04:12,540 --> 00:04:14,720
See, I knew you'd come up with something crafty.

49
00:04:15,620 --> 00:04:20,300
Never thought my sword would double as a shovel, but it got the job done way faster than I thought it would.

50
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:25,140
I have to admit, your speed was impressive, and you barely broke a sweat.

51
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:27,660
You pack a lot of muscle in that tiny frame.

52
00:04:28,260 --> 00:04:29,660
Hey, thanks, man. I've been training.

53
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:33,420
Now, this guy may be a fool, but he's strong.

54
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,000
No telling what he'll do when he wakes up.

55
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:38,860
Put a magic circle near the entrance, just in case.

56
00:04:39,660 --> 00:04:42,380
Whoa! So that's how you lay traps!

57
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:43,520
And they just disappear!

58
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:47,940
If anyone shows up and tries to rescue the fool, kaboom.

59
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:51,360
Might as well bury him while I'm at it.

60
00:04:51,820 --> 00:04:52,720
Can't be too careful.

61
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:55,660
Hey! That's overkill.

62
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:58,340
Not to mention my sword's down there with him.

63
00:04:58,480 --> 00:04:59,640
You hear that? This way!

64
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:01,840
I know that voice!

65
00:05:02,020 --> 00:05:05,380
Flame Reinforcement Magic Risky Stolen Pace!

66
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:07,460
Come on, come on, come on, come on, come on, come on!

67
00:05:07,460 --> 00:05:10,240
Oh, yeah! I found you, Crystal Hell!

68
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:12,100
You're really bringing the heat, huh, Magna?

69
00:05:12,660 --> 00:05:13,020
Huh.

70
00:05:14,380 --> 00:05:17,360
I know better than to get close enough for you to attack me, Asta.

71
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:20,980
But at this distance, I'm sure to win this match.

72
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:24,460
Call it revenge for what happened during your stupid baptism.

73
00:05:25,840 --> 00:05:29,680
Don't think that I haven't grown into a more powerful wizard than I was back then.

74
00:05:29,940 --> 00:05:32,480
You gotta prove it! Bring it on!

75
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:34,720
Take that!

76
00:05:38,300 --> 00:05:39,060
All right.

77
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:42,100
I can hit this back, no problem.

78
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:44,580
You're not gonna get this crystal, Magna!

79
00:05:44,580 --> 00:05:51,400
Uh-oh!

80
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:51,420
Uh-oh!

81
00:05:51,920 --> 00:05:52,180
Ah!

82
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:53,100
Ha-ha-ha-ha!

83
00:05:53,580 --> 00:05:55,120
That's a swing and a miss!

84
00:05:55,540 --> 00:05:59,560
My new Annihilation Massacre fireball vanishes before it ever hits its target.

85
00:06:00,020 --> 00:06:03,860
There's no way you can stop something that disappears right before your eyes.

86
00:06:04,220 --> 00:06:05,640
That's an awesome spell!

87
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:08,460
I shouldn't be surprised coming from Magna.

88
00:06:09,220 --> 00:06:09,660
Oh!

89
00:06:10,300 --> 00:06:11,340
Quite impressive!

90
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:13,860
Turns out he's more skilled than he looks.

91
00:06:14,580 --> 00:06:17,940
You should see him fire up the grill whenever we have a big barbecue!

92
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:23,100
If I try to get close to Magna, he'll just sprint away with that speedy spell from earlier.

93
00:06:23,760 --> 00:06:25,620
Plus, I'd be leaving the crystal wide open.

94
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:29,180
I'd need to go all black Asta to get close to him quickly.

95
00:06:29,620 --> 00:06:31,520
But that power's still cooling down.

96
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:33,580
Dang it.

97
00:06:33,580 --> 00:06:34,980
Mimosa!

98
00:06:35,580 --> 00:06:36,400
Where are you?

99
00:06:36,460 --> 00:06:37,240
I need your help!

100
00:06:37,260 --> 00:06:37,860
Hey, runt!

101
00:06:38,460 --> 00:06:39,780
Hold out for ten.

102
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:40,560
No.

103
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:42,720
Make that five minutes.

104
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:43,280
Sure.

105
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:44,460
I'm on it.

106
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:50,400
Hey!

107
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:52,140
Wait up, you thieving threat!

108
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:54,380
You see that, Mimosa?

109
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:57,960
Such a young child already devoted to a life of crime.

110
00:06:58,700 --> 00:06:59,280
Take note.

111
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:01,440
The poor are poor to their very souls.

112
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:03,400
Ugly outside and within.

113
00:07:04,020 --> 00:07:08,460
Those who are revolting in childhood are destined to be just as hideous when they're adults.

114
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:16,020
Hey!

115
00:07:16,300 --> 00:07:16,940
You okay?

116
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:18,640
Time to rise and shine!

117
00:07:19,780 --> 00:07:21,200
I said wake up!

118
00:07:21,200 --> 00:07:25,600
Good, you finally decided to join us.

119
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:29,980
I'm afraid I can never forgive you for laying a hand on my glorious face.

120
00:07:30,320 --> 00:07:33,500
Hate to tell you this, but it was pretty messed up before I got here.

121
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:35,680
My beautiful visage shall survive.

122
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:37,080
You are not beautiful.

123
00:07:38,500 --> 00:07:40,320
You're not deserving of that word.

124
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:42,800
It should only be used to describe people like Char.

125
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:59,340
Now then, we'll be back soon.

126
00:07:59,660 --> 00:08:01,120
Take care of the village while we're gone.

127
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:02,860
You can count on me.

128
00:08:03,380 --> 00:08:05,440
No reason to worry when I'm watching over things.

129
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:08,640
You focus on making money and I'll make sure everyone here's safe.

130
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:12,220
Just as I expected, you're still a heck of a spitfire, Saul.

131
00:08:13,080 --> 00:08:15,820
But this village is full of promising, reliable young men.

132
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,320
They'll handle things for us.

133
00:08:17,660 --> 00:08:18,300
That's right.

134
00:08:18,380 --> 00:08:19,560
We'll take care of everything.

135
00:08:20,060 --> 00:08:20,460
Yeah.

136
00:08:20,780 --> 00:08:23,080
We'll guard the village while our fathers are away.

137
00:08:23,380 --> 00:08:26,240
You be a good girl and go help our mothers out, why don't you?

138
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:26,680
What?

139
00:08:27,720 --> 00:08:31,880
Aren't you the baby who just spent the afternoon running around crying because a scary-looking

140
00:08:31,880 --> 00:08:33,340
stray dog wanted to lick him?

141
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:37,320
I'm way stronger than any of you little boys in town.

142
00:08:37,400 --> 00:08:38,580
Everyone knows it's true.

143
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:43,920
Maybe, but even if you are kind of strong for a girl, you're still just a woman, and

144
00:08:43,920 --> 00:08:45,980
us men are the ones who should be doing the protecting.

145
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:48,400
Wait, huh?

146
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:50,240
You really think that matters?

147
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:52,580
I am worried, though.

148
00:08:52,580 --> 00:08:56,920
We've heard reports that there are bandits wandering around targeting villages far from

149
00:08:56,920 --> 00:08:57,820
the royal capital.

150
00:08:58,340 --> 00:09:01,220
They attacked a rural village to the east not too long ago.

151
00:09:01,460 --> 00:09:02,760
There's no need to panic.

152
00:09:03,220 --> 00:09:06,980
Those bandits you heard about were all but destroyed thanks to the magic knights going

153
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:07,540
after them.

154
00:09:08,620 --> 00:09:11,940
If anything happens, you should contact the magic knights right away.

155
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:13,020
Goodbye for now.

156
00:09:13,180 --> 00:09:14,420
We'll be back before you know it.

157
00:09:22,580 --> 00:09:33,620
Grab anything that looks valuable, and any woman who looks like she might sell, and be

158
00:09:33,620 --> 00:09:34,380
quick about it.

159
00:09:34,780 --> 00:09:37,240
We've got to be gone before those damn knights show up.

160
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:39,480
Everyone needs to get to the church right now.

161
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:42,420
I know what you're thinking, but you can't stay out here.

162
00:09:42,500 --> 00:09:43,380
You have to come too.

163
00:09:43,620 --> 00:09:44,580
I'll be fine on my own.

164
00:09:44,640 --> 00:09:45,140
Just go.

165
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:47,640
Our guards, huh?

166
00:09:52,040 --> 00:09:53,440
Hey now, Missy.

167
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:55,280
This area's dangerous.

168
00:09:55,880 --> 00:09:57,800
Especially for a beauty like you.

169
00:09:58,280 --> 00:10:00,580
I'm betting you'll grow into a fine woman soon.

170
00:10:01,300 --> 00:10:03,020
You're gonna be joining us now.

171
00:10:03,620 --> 00:10:07,120
If you come quietly, I'll guarantee you'll only get bruised up a little bit.

172
00:10:07,860 --> 00:10:10,620
Leave this village immediately, or I'll force you out!

173
00:10:11,460 --> 00:10:13,260
She's a real wild one, isn't she?

174
00:10:13,260 --> 00:10:16,200
That's good, and I think they were just the men to tame her.

175
00:10:26,140 --> 00:10:28,260
Looks like we found a mouse in the alley.

176
00:10:28,880 --> 00:10:30,000
What's wrong, kid?

177
00:10:30,240 --> 00:10:31,980
You so scared you can't even run?

178
00:10:32,260 --> 00:10:33,200
You want to impress her?

179
00:10:33,820 --> 00:10:34,900
Here's a little tip.

180
00:10:34,980 --> 00:10:36,640
You'll have to do more than just stare.

181
00:10:37,500 --> 00:10:39,880
Why don't you come here and try to save your friend?

182
00:10:40,160 --> 00:10:42,460
I mean, unless you value your life.

183
00:10:43,260 --> 00:10:47,000
And us men are the ones who should be doing the protecting.

184
00:10:47,660 --> 00:10:48,540
Sorry, Sol.

185
00:10:49,500 --> 00:10:51,540
Well, so much for being rescued.

186
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:54,360
Not that he ever stood a chance against us.

187
00:10:54,780 --> 00:10:56,840
Forget about that hopeless kid, girly.

188
00:10:57,280 --> 00:10:59,440
I'll teach you how to play like a grown-up.

189
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:10,820
Captain Charlotte really went out of her way to protect a poor village like that.

190
00:11:12,340 --> 00:11:14,540
You remember what the Wizard King said.

191
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:17,560
We fight for people regardless of their rank or status.

192
00:11:18,220 --> 00:11:19,060
And Char?

193
00:11:19,680 --> 00:11:23,560
Not only did she save my life, she gave me a goal for the future, too.

194
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:27,340
Can you stand?

195
00:11:31,900 --> 00:11:33,380
There's no need to be afraid.

196
00:11:36,460 --> 00:11:37,560
I wasn't.

197
00:11:37,980 --> 00:11:39,120
I swear it.

198
00:11:39,120 --> 00:11:43,380
I really was planning to fight them and win.

199
00:11:43,820 --> 00:11:44,240
Somehow.

200
00:11:44,580 --> 00:11:45,020
Someway.

201
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:47,020
This is home.

202
00:11:47,780 --> 00:11:49,700
I wanted to protect everyone here.

203
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:53,120
But...

204
00:11:53,780 --> 00:11:55,520
I couldn't do anything.

205
00:11:56,180 --> 00:11:57,300
I was too weak.

206
00:11:57,300 --> 00:12:00,360
I'm so mad at myself.

207
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:03,300
I believed what those boys said about me,

208
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:05,280
even if it was just for a second.

209
00:12:06,240 --> 00:12:07,340
I'm a failure.

210
00:12:10,140 --> 00:12:11,380
What does it take?

211
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:13,560
How do I become a powerful person?

212
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:15,880
Please tell me!

213
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:22,820
How do I become strong and beautiful like you are?

214
00:12:22,820 --> 00:12:27,460
You are plenty beautiful already.

215
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:32,860
Moving forward, you should focus on training your body and your magic.

216
00:12:33,840 --> 00:12:35,460
You'll grow up to be powerful.

217
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:36,780
I'm sure of it.

218
00:12:38,060 --> 00:12:41,320
When that happens, I hope you'll join the Magic Knights.

219
00:12:41,640 --> 00:12:42,700
You think that I could?

220
00:12:43,820 --> 00:12:44,260
Seriously?

221
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:48,240
I'll be waiting with the Blue Rose Knights.

222
00:12:52,820 --> 00:13:01,640
They didn't take you.

223
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:02,900
You're fine.

224
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:03,940
You.

225
00:13:05,780 --> 00:13:06,780
Oh, Sol.

226
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:08,140
I'm sorry.

227
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:14,700
What are you apologizing for?

228
00:13:14,700 --> 00:13:18,120
I wasn't ever relying on you to save me, you idiot.

229
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:22,200
I'm sorry you had to see me looking so pitiful.

230
00:13:22,820 --> 00:13:25,880
I thought I could finish that bandit guy off with a single shot,

231
00:13:26,020 --> 00:13:27,420
but I guess I let my guard down.

232
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:30,280
Don't worry about it, though.

233
00:13:30,340 --> 00:13:33,440
If they show up again, I swear I'll keep you in this village safe,

234
00:13:33,520 --> 00:13:34,380
no matter what.

235
00:13:34,700 --> 00:13:35,240
Of course.

236
00:13:36,040 --> 00:13:37,060
Then it's decided.

237
00:13:37,580 --> 00:13:39,240
I'll get stronger and stronger,

238
00:13:39,460 --> 00:13:41,060
and I'll join the Magic Knights.

239
00:13:41,860 --> 00:13:42,820
And then...

240
00:13:44,820 --> 00:13:50,880
What was her name?

241
00:13:50,880 --> 00:13:53,420
Never mind.

242
00:13:54,860 --> 00:13:55,740
Wait for me.

243
00:13:56,420 --> 00:13:57,480
Whoever you are.

244
00:14:00,100 --> 00:14:03,580
Don't you have a reason to overcome your narcissism and win this fight?

245
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:04,780
Or are you weak?

246
00:14:04,780 --> 00:14:06,780
Gah...

247
00:14:06,780 --> 00:14:12,580
Crap, missed again!

248
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:14,880
Hitting a tiny target is hard enough,

249
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:17,220
but at that speed, I can't even sense their key.

250
00:14:17,980 --> 00:14:22,260
I don't have some kind of fancy-schmancy anti-magic sword like he does,

251
00:14:22,640 --> 00:14:24,000
and I'm definitely no noble.

252
00:14:24,480 --> 00:14:26,060
If I was, this wouldn't be a problem

253
00:14:26,060 --> 00:14:28,300
because I could fire off a million high-powered spells.

254
00:14:28,300 --> 00:14:31,520
But I do have this sure-to-hit technical magic.

255
00:14:31,980 --> 00:14:33,660
The blast might be small,

256
00:14:34,220 --> 00:14:36,740
but this is how I can overcome him in a fight!

257
00:14:42,040 --> 00:14:42,880
Wait, what?

258
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:44,080
Finally!

259
00:14:44,260 --> 00:14:45,600
About time I stopped one!

260
00:14:46,040 --> 00:14:46,860
What's the matter?

261
00:14:46,980 --> 00:14:48,080
Keep them coming, Magna!

262
00:14:48,080 --> 00:14:49,920
Ah, you asked for it!

263
00:14:50,120 --> 00:14:51,240
Feel the heat!

264
00:14:52,460 --> 00:14:52,940
Dang.

265
00:14:53,660 --> 00:14:55,160
He's putting up a heck of a fight.

266
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:57,480
I'm barely scoring any hits now.

267
00:14:58,440 --> 00:15:00,620
I'm still letting too many of them through.

268
00:15:01,680 --> 00:15:03,360
The crystal's not looking too good.

269
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:05,480
Magna really is amazing!

270
00:15:06,520 --> 00:15:08,140
That's such an intense match-up,

271
00:15:08,180 --> 00:15:09,440
I can't take my eyes off them!

272
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:11,920
And it's only going to get better.

273
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:14,200
Neither of those two knows how to hold back.

274
00:15:14,740 --> 00:15:16,760
Oh, man, I bet they're having so much fun!

275
00:15:16,920 --> 00:15:18,360
I can't wait to get back out there!

276
00:15:18,700 --> 00:15:20,540
Come on, guys, finish up your match!

277
00:15:21,680 --> 00:15:22,120
Basta!

278
00:15:22,740 --> 00:15:25,120
You really are something, you stupid twerp!

279
00:15:25,740 --> 00:15:27,540
Thank you...

280
00:15:27,540 --> 00:15:29,800
for making not just me,

281
00:15:30,120 --> 00:15:31,320
but all of us stronger,

282
00:15:31,420 --> 00:15:32,600
you little jerkwad!

283
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:34,520
But just so you know,

284
00:15:35,260 --> 00:15:36,900
the final isn't gonna be

285
00:15:36,900 --> 00:15:38,680
between you and that you-know guy!

286
00:15:39,620 --> 00:15:41,480
It's between me and Locke!

287
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:45,540
Seems you're forgetting about this dashing mage!

288
00:15:45,660 --> 00:15:47,760
Oh, man, I thought we were done with this guy!

289
00:15:47,980 --> 00:15:48,860
There we are.

290
00:15:50,460 --> 00:15:52,920
It's criminal to mar such a beautiful face!

291
00:15:53,300 --> 00:15:55,020
And punishable by death!

292
00:15:55,420 --> 00:15:55,860
Yikes!

293
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:56,840
Two against one!

294
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:57,560
Not good!

295
00:15:58,280 --> 00:15:59,500
And it looks like our crystal

296
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:00,680
could shatter any second!

297
00:16:01,120 --> 00:16:01,920
What do I do?

298
00:16:02,620 --> 00:16:04,380
Go after the flower guy!

299
00:16:04,860 --> 00:16:05,680
Do it now!

300
00:16:05,680 --> 00:16:13,540
It's true that I can't see your fireballs

301
00:16:13,540 --> 00:16:14,620
