310
00:16:32,020 --> 00:16:34,440
Well, this just proves

311
00:16:34,440 --> 00:16:36,460
that my magic is awesome!

312
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:39,880
Magic is the essence of beauty

313
00:16:39,880 --> 00:16:41,560
and that sword wipes it out.

314
00:16:42,100 --> 00:16:43,160
This is appalling.

315
00:16:44,020 --> 00:16:46,260
His power is in the front to my senses.

316
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:49,400
I shall no longer simply scorn you!

317
00:16:50,020 --> 00:16:50,840
Lowly Commodore!

318
00:16:51,340 --> 00:16:52,480
Instead, I shall destroy

319
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:53,500
every trace of you

320
00:16:53,500 --> 00:16:54,440
and your crystal!

321
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:55,540
Uh-oh!

322
00:16:55,880 --> 00:16:57,080
If he goes any higher,

323
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:58,580
forget fighting off his blossoms!

324
00:16:59,040 --> 00:17:00,720
I won't be able to land any attack!

325
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:02,600
Our crystal will be history!

326
00:17:03,500 --> 00:17:05,820
I don't care how unseemly it is!

327
00:17:05,920 --> 00:17:07,420
I'm using all my power!

328
00:17:08,620 --> 00:17:09,180
What?

329
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:11,920
Ensnared by some kind of magic?

330
00:17:12,120 --> 00:17:12,560
Bingo.

331
00:17:13,520 --> 00:17:14,860
I set plenty of traps

332
00:17:14,860 --> 00:17:16,800
up in the sky, too, by the way.

333
00:17:17,220 --> 00:17:18,360
Maybe you should have focused

334
00:17:18,360 --> 00:17:19,980
on your trademark magic sensing

335
00:17:19,980 --> 00:17:21,440
instead of talking trash.

336
00:17:22,720 --> 00:17:24,940
This will only slow me for a moment!

337
00:17:25,240 --> 00:17:26,360
That's all I need

338
00:17:26,360 --> 00:17:27,460
to beat you!

339
00:17:27,460 --> 00:17:33,000
Jeez, man.

340
00:17:33,540 --> 00:17:35,300
Knocked out twice in one match?

341
00:17:36,560 --> 00:17:38,600
You're gonna feel so humiliated

342
00:17:38,600 --> 00:17:39,540
when you wake up.

343
00:17:41,540 --> 00:17:43,020
It's K-Dot time!

344
00:17:43,280 --> 00:17:45,000
This is the end of the line for you!

345
00:17:46,080 --> 00:17:46,800
Oh, no!

346
00:17:46,880 --> 00:17:47,400
The crystal!

347
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:51,440
Huh?

348
00:17:51,780 --> 00:17:53,420
Hey, what's going on, stupid?

349
00:17:53,780 --> 00:17:55,020
We almost got them!

350
00:17:55,020 --> 00:18:00,720
I did it!

351
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:02,440
Just in time!

352
00:18:02,640 --> 00:18:04,020
Whoa, nice one, Mimosa!

353
00:18:04,700 --> 00:18:06,440
Hey, wake up!

354
00:18:06,620 --> 00:18:07,880
Do what I tell you to!

355
00:18:08,280 --> 00:18:08,780
Ah!

356
00:18:10,900 --> 00:18:11,460
Huh?

357
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:12,040
No!

358
00:18:12,420 --> 00:18:14,240
That's the opposite of what I want!

359
00:18:15,240 --> 00:18:16,620
Here we go!

360
00:18:16,620 --> 00:18:16,980
Oh!

361
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:21,620
Crystal destroyed!

362
00:18:22,020 --> 00:18:23,480
Oh, so cool!

363
00:18:23,480 --> 00:18:24,800
Team B wins!

364
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:25,420
Whoa!

365
00:18:26,020 --> 00:18:27,640
Now that was a fun match!

366
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:29,940
Magna and Asta are both so cool!

367
00:18:30,320 --> 00:18:32,100
Our boys really hustled out there.

368
00:18:32,380 --> 00:18:34,060
I guess we'll have to drink a toast to them

369
00:18:34,060 --> 00:18:35,240
when this is all wrapped up.

370
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:37,520
Only real friends can fight so right

371
00:18:37,520 --> 00:18:40,240
and sleep Magna and Asta are fight friends.

372
00:18:40,320 --> 00:18:41,480
Oh, heck yeah!

373
00:18:41,740 --> 00:18:42,780
We did it!

374
00:18:43,040 --> 00:18:44,280
Nice job, Snazzy Mask!

375
00:18:44,980 --> 00:18:46,220
Not that I'm surprised,

376
00:18:46,340 --> 00:18:48,800
because teamwork always gets the job done in a fight.

377
00:18:49,660 --> 00:18:50,200
Oh, yeah!

378
00:18:50,360 --> 00:18:51,760
Bring it in for a high five!

379
00:18:51,760 --> 00:18:54,560
So it all played out like you thought it would.

380
00:18:54,740 --> 00:18:55,840
You could hear me right here!

381
00:18:56,160 --> 00:18:57,040
Stop facing out on me!

382
00:18:57,040 --> 00:18:58,660
It would have been much easier to win

383
00:18:58,660 --> 00:19:01,540
if you hadn't destroyed my traps in the beginning, moron.

384
00:19:01,820 --> 00:19:02,920
You're mad about that?

385
00:19:03,320 --> 00:19:05,140
Can't we just high-five this out, huh?

386
00:19:05,380 --> 00:19:05,860
Please?

387
00:19:06,120 --> 00:19:07,480
I'm starting to feel kind of stupid in here!

388
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:09,740
Maybe you'd like a little advice from the victors.

389
00:19:10,100 --> 00:19:10,680
Let's see.

390
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:12,800
The Azure Amazon.

391
00:19:12,800 --> 00:19:16,200
You're good, but you got sloppy out there.

392
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:20,020
If you'd been a little more attuned to the subtleties of magic power,

393
00:19:20,460 --> 00:19:21,640
you might not have lost.

394
00:19:22,580 --> 00:19:26,500
This detonating delinquent spent way too much of his mana during the warm-up.

395
00:19:27,080 --> 00:19:28,780
Maybe it's a habit for commoners,

396
00:19:28,880 --> 00:19:31,280
but you've got to learn how to say when.

397
00:19:31,280 --> 00:19:34,540
And there's you, the royal narcissist.

398
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:38,240
You were far too arrogant the entire time.

399
00:19:39,040 --> 00:19:42,920
Falling to pieces just because you got punched by someone you see as lower than you?

400
00:19:43,700 --> 00:19:46,020
That makes you the ugliest one of all.

401
00:19:46,740 --> 00:19:47,900
What is with you?

402
00:19:47,960 --> 00:19:50,180
You're going way too far with these burns again!

403
00:19:50,480 --> 00:19:51,920
Wouldn't kill you to be nicer!

404
00:19:52,740 --> 00:19:53,140
Brother.

405
00:19:54,440 --> 00:19:55,000
Mimosa.

406
00:19:55,780 --> 00:19:57,080
What you said back then.

407
00:19:58,060 --> 00:20:02,760
Sometimes it is true that a commoner's impoverished condition can lead their soul to ruin.

408
00:20:03,280 --> 00:20:03,840
I agree.

409
00:20:07,800 --> 00:20:12,280
But true beauty is something even poverty can't take away.

410
00:20:12,840 --> 00:20:14,440
It lives inside of them.

411
00:20:17,120 --> 00:20:18,300
Avert your eyes.

412
00:20:19,560 --> 00:20:20,700
You mustn't look at me.

413
00:20:20,700 --> 00:20:22,300
I'm hideous.

414
00:20:24,660 --> 00:20:27,420
You did lose in a rather unsightly manner.

415
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:29,120
But think about it.

416
00:20:29,180 --> 00:20:31,440
Not only did you accept that commoners can be mighty,

417
00:20:31,560 --> 00:20:33,680
you fought beside them, getting yourself dirty.

418
00:20:34,220 --> 00:20:36,920
Honestly, this is the most beautiful you've ever been.

419
00:20:38,900 --> 00:20:41,080
I certainly don't want to admit this.

420
00:20:41,600 --> 00:20:42,580
But it's true.

421
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:46,400
They really were gorgeous.

422
00:20:46,400 --> 00:20:51,240
Royalty losing to these peasants?

423
00:20:51,320 --> 00:20:52,700
How downright deplorable!

424
00:20:53,860 --> 00:20:54,760
Next up.

425
00:20:55,080 --> 00:20:55,680
Round two.

426
00:20:55,940 --> 00:20:56,520
Match two.

427
00:20:57,060 --> 00:20:57,940
Prepare yourselves.

428
00:20:58,940 --> 00:21:00,120
It's my turn.

429
00:21:01,120 --> 00:21:02,720
And I won't lose.

430
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:05,300
You got that, Longris?

431
00:21:05,340 --> 00:21:06,600
Processing by Chancellor.

432
00:21:06,600 --> 00:21:06,940
I promise you.

433
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:08,240
I know.

434
00:21:20,300 --> 00:21:20,900
Bye.

435
00:21:20,900 --> 00:21:22,140
Chapter 2.

436
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:23,020
Later.

437
00:21:23,020 --> 00:21:23,840
Let's go.

438
00:21:23,900 --> 00:21:24,160
Let's go.

439
00:21:24,160 --> 00:21:24,660
Let's go.

440
00:21:24,760 --> 00:21:25,940
Let's go.

441
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:28,060
Let's start.

442
00:21:28,160 --> 00:21:28,760
Let's go.

443
00:21:28,820 --> 00:21:30,060
Let's go.

444
00:21:30,280 --> 00:21:30,720
Let's go.

445
00:21:30,760 --> 00:21:30,840
Hey.

446
00:21:30,840 --> 00:21:31,840
Buy progressive.

447
00:21:31,900 --> 00:21:32,980
You got it.

448
00:21:32,980 --> 00:22:02,960
Thank you.

449
00:22:02,980 --> 00:22:32,960
Thank you.

450
00:22:32,980 --> 00:22:34,980
Thank you.

451
00:23:02,980 --> 00:23:04,980
Thank you.

452
00:23:04,980 --> 00:23:07,420
And she'd never be able to accept such a wimp.

453
00:23:08,460 --> 00:23:12,220
The Wizard King does seem like that rare, acceptable man.

454
00:23:12,580 --> 00:23:13,840
But he loves everybody.

455
00:23:14,420 --> 00:23:16,340
Char needs someone who will love only her.

456
00:23:17,320 --> 00:23:20,980
So someone who's taller than Char, not a punk or gaudy or a narcissist,

457
00:23:21,200 --> 00:23:24,520
who can pleasantly chat with her is stronger and will love her and her alone.

458
00:23:24,680 --> 00:23:25,100
Let's see.

459
00:23:25,160 --> 00:23:27,920
There's got to be someone I know who matches that description perfectly.

460
00:23:27,920 --> 00:23:32,180
The obvious choice has got to be me!

461
00:23:32,460 --> 00:23:33,240
Come here, Char!

462
00:23:36,080 --> 00:23:38,920
Finral's up against his little brother Longris in the next match.

463
00:23:39,200 --> 00:23:40,740
Come on, Finral, believe in yourself!

464
00:23:41,600 --> 00:23:42,940
Black Clover, page 80.

465
00:23:43,240 --> 00:23:45,560
Special little brother versus failed big brother.

466
00:23:46,400 --> 00:23:48,340
Finral, you are not gonna lose this one!

467
00:23:48,340 --> 00:23:48,480
Bye now!

